  "result": "I implemented `satisfies(version, range)` in `src/semver.js` following `docs/SPEC.md`, and `npm test` passes (4 passed, 0 failed).\n\nI added `test/satisfies.test.js`, which checks examples from every section of the spec: x-ranges, operators on partial versions, tilde, caret, hyphen ranges, `||` sets, prerelease ordering and the same-tuple prerelease rule. It also checks that invalid versions and ranges return `false` without throwing.\n\nSome behaviors the spec doesn't state, which I chose:\n- **Wildcard operators:** `>*` and `<*` match nothing, while `>=*` and `<=*` match any non-prerelease version.\n- **Partial versions:** a prerelease on a partial version (e.g. `1.2-beta`) is invalid.\n- **Wildcards:** anything after a wildcard is treated as a wildcard, so `1.x.3` means `1.x`.\n- **Operators:** whitespace after `~` or `^` is accepted, as it is for the other operators.\n- **Bad `||` sets:** if any `||` set is malformed, the whole range is invalid and returns `false`.",
